                            </svg>

                        </div>

                        <p class="image-caption">

                            One JavaScript file can export code and another
                            JavaScript file can import and reuse it.

                        </p>

                    </div>


                    <!-- =================================================
                         HOW MODULES WORK
                         ================================================= -->

                    <div class="diagram-box">

                        <div class="diagram-title">
                            How JavaScript Modules Work
                        </div>

                        <div class="diagram-row">

                            <div class="diagram-item">
                                Create Module
                            </div>

                            <div class="diagram-arrow">
                                →
                            </div>

                            <div class="diagram-item main">
                                export
                            </div>

                            <div class="diagram-arrow">
                                →
                            </div>

                            <div class="diagram-item green">
                                import
                            </div>

                            <div class="diagram-arrow">
                                →
                            </div>

                            <div class="diagram-item">
                                Reuse Code
                            </div>

                        </div>

                    </div>


                    <!-- =================================================
                         EXPORT
                         ================================================= -->

                    <h2 class="section-title">
                        Export
                    </h2>

                    <p class="section-text">

                        The <strong>export</strong> keyword makes a
                        variable, function, or class available to
                        other JavaScript modules.

                    </p>

                    <pre class="code-box"><code>export function add(a, b) {
    return a + b;
}</code></pre>

                    <div class="try-it-wrapper">

                        <button type="button"
                                class="try-it-btn"
                                onclick="tryModulesExample1()">

                            ▶ Try It

                        </button>

                    </div>

                    <div class="output-box">

                        Function exported successfully.

                    </div>


                    <!-- =================================================
                         IMPORT
                         ================================================= -->

                    <h2 class="section-title">
                        Import
                    </h2>

                    <p class="section-text">

                        The <strong>import</strong> keyword is used to
                        use exported code inside another JavaScript
                        module.

                    </p>

                    <pre class="code-box"><code>import { add } from "./math.js";

let result = add(10, 20);

console.log(result);</code></pre>

                    <div class="try-it-wrapper">

                        <button type="button"
                                class="try-it-btn"
                                onclick="tryModulesExample2()">

                            ▶ Try It

                        </button>

                    </div>

                    <div class="output-box">

                        30

                    </div>


                    <!-- =================================================
                         NAMED EXPORT
                         ================================================= -->

                    <h2 class="section-title">
                        Named Export
                    </h2>

                    <p class="section-text">

                        Multiple variables or functions can be exported
                        from the same module.

                    </p>

                    <pre class="code-box"><code>export const name = "Rahul";

export function greet() {
    return "Hello " + name;
}</code></pre>

                    <div class="try-it-wrapper">

                        <button type="button"
                                class="try-it-btn"
                                onclick="tryModulesExample3()">

                            ▶ Try It

                        </button>

                    </div>

                    <div class="output-box">

                        Hello Rahul

                    </div>


                    <!-- =================================================
                         DEFAULT EXPORT
                         ================================================= -->

                    <h2 class="section-title">
                        Default Export
                    </h2>

                    <p class="section-text">

                        A module can have one default export.

                    </p>

                    <pre class="code-box"><code>export default function greet() {
    return "Welcome to CIIT Training Institute";
}</code></pre>

                    <div class="try-it-wrapper">

                        <button type="button"
                                class="try-it-btn"
                                onclick="tryModulesExample4()">

                            ▶ Try It

                        </button>

                    </div>

                    <div class="output-box">

                        Welcome to CIIT Training Institute

                    </div>


                    <!-- =================================================
                         BENEFITS
                         ================================================= -->

                    <h2 class="section-title">
                        Benefits of JavaScript Modules
                    </h2>

                    <div class="comparison-wrapper">

                        <table class="comparison-table">

                            <thead>

                                <tr>
                                    <th>Benefit</th>
                                    <th>Description</th>
                                </tr>

                            </thead>

                            <tbody>

                                <tr>
                                    <td>Code Organization</td>
                                    <td>
                                        Divides large applications into
                                        smaller files.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>

                                <tr>
                                    <td>Code Reusability</td>
                                    <td>
                                        Code can be imported and reused.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>

                                <tr>
                                    <td>Maintainability</td>
                                    <td>
                                        Smaller files are easier to manage.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>

                                <tr>
                                    <td>Separation</td>
                                    <td>
                                        Different parts of an application
                                        can be kept separate.
                                    </td>
                                </tr>

                            </tbody>

                        </table>

                    </div>


                    <!-- =================================================
                         IMPORTANT POINTS
                         ================================================= -->

                    <div class="concept-box">

                        <h5>
                            Important Points
                        </h5>

                        <p>
                            • <strong>export</strong> makes code available
                            to another module.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            • <strong>import</strong> brings exported code
                            into another module.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            • Modules help organize large applications.
                        </p>

                        <p class="mb-0">
                            • Modules improve code reusability and
                            maintainability.
                        </p>

                    </div>


                    <!-- =================================================
                         SUMMARY
                         ================================================= -->

                    <div class="summary-box">

                        <h2 class="h4">
                            Summary
                        </h2>

                        <p>

                            JavaScript Modules allow developers to split
                            code into separate files. The
                            <strong>export</strong> keyword shares code
                            from a module, while the
                            <strong>import</strong> keyword allows another
                            module to use that code.

                        </p>

                    </div>


                    <!-- =================================================
                         BOTTOM NAVIGATION
                         ================================================= -->

                    <div class="bottom-navigation">

                        <a href="@Url.Action("SpreadRest", "ModernJavaScript", new { area = "JavaScript" })"
